WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.066 --> 00:00:02.102
Call for an investigation of the Fed,

00:00:02.268 --> 00:00:04.004
arguing that Jerome Powell has failed.

00:00:04.004 --> 00:00:06.039
Now his defenders say

00:00:06.039 --> 00:00:07.874
the pandemic was a black swan event

00:00:07.874 --> 00:00:09.809
that sent the economy into a tailspin.

00:00:09.809 --> 00:00:10.844
And he has correctly read

00:00:10.844 --> 00:00:11.611
the labor markets

00:00:11.611 --> 00:00:12.679
ability to sustain

00:00:12.679 --> 00:00:13.313
full employment

00:00:13.313 --> 00:00:14.681
in the face of rate hikes.

00:00:14.681 --> 00:00:15.348
What do you say

00:00:15.348 --> 00:00:16.282
to those who argue,

00:00:16.282 --> 00:00:17.517
who disagree with you and argue?

00:00:17.517 --> 00:00:18.151
POWELL

00:00:18.151 --> 00:00:20.120
Since this unprecedented

00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:21.388
cataclysmic economic

00:00:21.388 --> 00:00:22.589
event of the pandemic,

00:00:22.589 --> 00:00:24.424
that he's actually done a decent job?

00:00:24.424 --> 00:00:25.291
Well, you know,

00:00:25.291 --> 00:00:26.359
if you want to treat this

00:00:26.359 --> 00:00:27.961
as a cataclysmic event,

00:00:27.961 --> 00:00:30.196
which certainly the pandemic was,

00:00:30.196 --> 00:00:33.333
keep in mind it drove inflation in ways

00:00:33.633 --> 00:00:34.334
that are different

00:00:34.334 --> 00:00:35.769
from how we usually have it.

00:00:35.769 --> 00:00:37.103
So, for example,

00:00:37.103 --> 00:00:38.271
we have seen supply

00:00:38.271 --> 00:00:40.440
chain kinks that have driven up prices.

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:41.374
Then add to that

00:00:41.374 --> 00:00:43.143
we have a war in Ukraine.

00:00:43.143 --> 00:00:45.111
And then one of the big pieces

00:00:45.111 --> 00:00:46.846
has been a lot of price gouging.

00:00:46.846 --> 00:00:48.782
We've seen these giant corporations,

00:00:48.782 --> 00:00:49.949
particularly in industries

00:00:49.949 --> 00:00:51.384
that are very concentrated,

00:00:51.384 --> 00:00:53.386
really pushing their prices up.

00:00:53.753 --> 00:00:55.221
So there are three things

00:00:55.221 --> 00:00:56.723
that are helping push prices up.

00:00:56.723 --> 00:00:58.591
And do you know how many of those three

00:00:58.591 --> 00:00:59.292
can be affected

00:00:59.292 --> 00:01:01.361
by raising interest rates? None of them.

00:01:01.861 --> 00:01:04.431
The whole point is that Powell is using

00:01:04.731 --> 00:01:06.833
the one tool the Fed has,

00:01:06.833 --> 00:01:09.302
and that is raise interest rates.

00:01:09.302 --> 00:01:12.005
But he has said himself in hearings,

00:01:12.138 --> 00:01:12.739
nope,

00:01:12.739 --> 00:01:14.908
it won't affect any of those things.

00:01:15.175 --> 00:01:17.277
But here's what it will effect.

00:01:17.277 --> 00:01:18.711
When the Fed uses language

00:01:18.711 --> 00:01:20.980
like we're trying to cool the economy

00:01:20.980 --> 00:01:23.516
or slow down the economy,

00:01:23.516 --> 00:01:25.819
the translation behind that is

00:01:26.453 --> 00:01:28.188
we're trying to increase unemployment.

00:01:28.188 --> 00:01:28.655
Right.

00:01:28.655 --> 00:01:29.222
And in fact,

00:01:29.222 --> 00:01:30.957
the Fed has said this

00:01:30.957 --> 00:01:32.025
in the last hearing

00:01:32.025 --> 00:01:32.959
that I have with

00:01:32.959 --> 00:01:34.294
with Chair Powell,

00:01:34.294 --> 00:01:35.962
when we had him in front of us

00:01:35.962 --> 00:01:37.363
and the Finance Committee,

00:01:37.363 --> 00:01:40.133
I looked at the Fed's own

00:01:40.133 --> 00:01:42.569
predictions, their report in December,

00:01:42.569 --> 00:01:45.205
in which they said, we want to keep

00:01:45.905 --> 00:01:48.475
trying to slow down the economy.

00:01:48.475 --> 00:01:50.910
And what we're hoping for out of this

00:01:51.411 --> 00:01:54.080
is that we increase unemployment

00:01:54.481 --> 00:01:57.083
by 2 million jobs.

00:01:57.417 --> 00:02:00.653
Now, that's a lot of people for whom

00:02:00.653 --> 00:02:01.721
that's a lot of hurt.

00:02:01.721 --> 00:02:02.856
These are people right now

00:02:02.856 --> 00:02:04.457
who are paying the rent,

00:02:04.457 --> 00:02:05.959
putting groceries on the table.

00:02:05.959 --> 00:02:07.927
They're not and they're not hiding this.

00:02:07.927 --> 00:02:09.028
They're saying this. He said it today.

00:02:09.028 --> 00:02:10.730
I think more than a million jobs

00:02:10.730 --> 00:02:12.031
to be lost this year

00:02:12.031 --> 00:02:13.199
because of these rate hikes.

00:02:13.199 --> 00:02:13.633
That's right.

00:02:13.633 --> 00:02:14.134
And actually,

00:02:14.134 --> 00:02:15.235
by the Fed's own production,

00:02:15.235 --> 00:02:17.237
it's more than 2 million.

00:02:17.237 --> 00:02:19.339
That is their target here.

00:02:19.906 --> 00:02:21.641
And the point I want to make is

00:02:21.641 --> 00:02:23.076
that's not going to help us on supply

00:02:23.076 --> 00:02:23.510
chain.

00:02:23.510 --> 00:02:25.778
It's not going to help us on the war

00:02:26.212 --> 00:02:26.980
in Ukraine.

00:02:26.980 --> 00:02:29.949
It's not going to help us on these

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:31.251
the price gouging

00:02:31.251 --> 00:02:33.219
from these big corporations.

00:02:33.219 --> 00:02:35.788
So I think we ought to be not doing the

00:02:36.322 --> 00:02:38.625
extra ordinary, these extreme

00:02:38.625 --> 00:02:39.859
interest rate hikes.

00:02:39.859 --> 00:02:41.227
We've never seen hikes

00:02:41.227 --> 00:02:44.531
at this rate in the modern economy

00:02:45.098 --> 00:02:46.900
and bearing down harder

00:02:46.900 --> 00:02:48.635
on these other costs

00:02:48.635 --> 00:02:50.403
that are these other factors

00:02:50.403 --> 00:02:51.104
that are driving up.

00:02:51.104 --> 00:02:52.205
But you think Fed Chair

00:02:52.205 --> 00:02:53.673
Powell should be doing things

00:02:53.673 --> 00:02:55.241
about these other things are,

00:02:55.241 --> 00:02:57.210
I think, what he should say.

00:02:57.210 --> 00:02:58.711
He should call, for example,

00:02:58.711 --> 00:03:02.715
for more on price gouging, but back off

00:03:03.016 --> 00:03:05.852
using his tool and keep trying to say

00:03:06.152 --> 00:03:06.486
that he's

00:03:06.486 --> 00:03:07.487
going to keep using it

00:03:07.487 --> 00:03:08.521
until he puts 2 million

00:03:08.521 --> 00:03:09.422
people out of work.

00:03:09.422 --> 00:03:10.190
So a December

00:03:10.190 --> 00:03:10.890
Washington Post

00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:11.558
column said

00:03:11.558 --> 00:03:13.359
that this is not the Warren presidency,

00:03:13.359 --> 00:03:13.693
but it's

00:03:13.693 --> 00:03:15.862
certainly a Warren infused

00:03:15.862 --> 00:03:16.930
presidency, meaning

00:03:16.930 --> 00:03:18.131
that the president, President Biden,

00:03:18.131 --> 00:03:20.166
is taking a lot of your suggestions

00:03:20.166 --> 00:03:21.901
and trying to enact them into law.

00:03:21.901 --> 00:03:23.937
Have you ever directly told

00:03:23.937 --> 00:03:25.338
President Biden

00:03:25.338 --> 00:03:27.373
that you think you should fire

00:03:27.373 --> 00:03:29.209
the chair, fire Jerome Powell?

00:03:29.209 --> 00:03:31.110
And who would you like to see

00:03:31.110 --> 00:03:32.245
replace him?

00:03:32.245 --> 00:03:33.513
So I'm not going to talk

00:03:33.513 --> 00:03:35.615
about private conversations,

00:03:35.615 --> 00:03:37.317
but what I will say is

00:03:37.317 --> 00:03:38.885
I've made it very clear

00:03:38.885 --> 00:03:41.521
as publicly as humanly possible

00:03:42.021 --> 00:03:43.056
that I didn't think

00:03:43.056 --> 00:03:44.257
that he should be

00:03:44.257 --> 00:03:46.292
reconfirmed as president,

00:03:46.292 --> 00:03:48.061
as chair of the Fed.

00:03:48.061 --> 00:03:49.028
And I think he's doing

00:03:49.028 --> 00:03:50.630
a really terrible job,

00:03:50.630 --> 00:03:51.831
and he's doing a terrible job

00:03:51.831 --> 00:03:53.433
on both fronts.

00:03:53.433 --> 00:03:55.501
Remember, there are two only two jobs

00:03:55.602 --> 00:03:56.869
for the Federal Reserve chair.

00:03:56.869 --> 00:03:59.005
One is monetary policy, inflation.

00:03:59.372 --> 00:04:01.507
I think he's doing a very bad job there.

00:04:01.507 --> 00:04:03.209
And it's risking

00:04:03.209 --> 00:04:05.645
pushing our economy into a recession.

00:04:06.212 --> 00:04:09.182
His other job is regulatory oversight,

00:04:09.515 --> 00:04:11.918
and he has spent five years

00:04:12.318 --> 00:04:14.153
weakening regulations

00:04:14.153 --> 00:04:16.356
over these multibillion dollar banks.

00:04:16.723 --> 00:04:17.423
I predicted

00:04:17.423 --> 00:04:18.191
five years ago

00:04:18.191 --> 00:04:20.526
the consequence of that kind of weakening

00:04:21.027 --> 00:04:23.096
would be that we would see these banks

00:04:23.329 --> 00:04:23.997
load up on

00:04:23.997 --> 00:04:24.764
risk, build

00:04:24.764 --> 00:04:26.299
their short term profits,

00:04:26.299 --> 00:04:28.801
give themselves ginormous

00:04:29.836 --> 00:04:30.903
bonuses and

00:04:30.903 --> 00:04:32.272
big salaries,

00:04:32.272 --> 00:04:33.506
and then some of those banks

00:04:33.506 --> 00:04:34.173
will explode.

00:04:34.173 --> 00:04:36.542
And that is exactly what has happened.

00:04:36.809 --> 00:04:37.410
On Share.

00:04:37.410 --> 00:04:37.910
Powell

00:04:37.910 --> 00:04:38.845
what you just mentioned,

00:04:38.845 --> 00:04:40.079
the prospect of a recession.

00:04:40.079 --> 00:04:41.414
Do you think the United States

00:04:41.414 --> 00:04:42.915
is headed for a recession?

00:04:42.915 --> 00:04:44.784
I think that that is where Jerome Powell

00:04:44.784 --> 00:04:45.785
is trying to drive it.

00:04:45.785 --> 00:04:47.253
And he's got two different ways

00:04:47.253 --> 00:04:47.987
because he's purposely

00:04:47.987 --> 00:04:49.389
trying to drive it to a recession.

00:04:49.389 --> 00:04:51.257
Well, what he's trying to do is get 2

00:04:51.257 --> 00:04:52.558
million people laid off.

00:04:52.558 --> 00:04:53.660
And one of the things

00:04:53.660 --> 00:04:55.461
that we need to understand

00:04:55.461 --> 00:04:57.930
when he wants to raise the unemployment

00:04:57.930 --> 00:04:59.799
rate by more than a point

00:04:59.799 --> 00:05:02.035
within a single 12 month period.

00:05:02.835 --> 00:05:04.804
We have done that before in this country.

00:05:04.804 --> 00:05:07.940
In fact, we have done it 12 times before.

00:05:07.940 --> 00:05:09.976
And out of all 12 times,

00:05:10.310 --> 00:05:11.277
how many times has

00:05:11.277 --> 00:05:13.413
it resulted in a recession?

00:05:13.413 --> 00:05:15.281
The answer is 12.

00:05:15.281 --> 00:05:16.983
So that's the direction

00:05:16.983 --> 00:05:18.184
he's trying to push this.

00:05:18.184 --> 00:05:20.219
That is a danger to our economy.

00:05:20.486 --> 00:05:22.055
It's why I said five years ago,

00:05:22.055 --> 00:05:23.289
I think he's a dangerous man

00:05:23.289 --> 00:05:24.157
to have in this job.

00:05:24.157 --> 00:05:26.426
So CNN has exclusively obtained

00:05:26.426 --> 00:05:26.893
a letter written

00:05:26.893 --> 00:05:28.294
by you and six other senators

00:05:28.294 --> 00:05:29.128
after the collapse

00:05:29.128 --> 00:05:30.296
of the Silicon Valley Bank.

00:05:30.296 --> 00:05:32.131
You're calling for the Fed to crack down

00:05:32.131 --> 00:05:34.133
on these large regional banks, arguing

00:05:34.133 --> 00:05:35.001
that they cannot be left

00:05:35.001 --> 00:05:36.469
to supervise themselves.

00:05:36.469 --> 00:05:37.203
As you know,

00:05:37.203 --> 00:05:39.939
Powell is not the only banking regulator.

00:05:40.506 --> 00:05:43.509
It's the Oxy, the S.E.C., FINRA, the

00:05:44.043 --> 00:05:45.311
the CFP,

00:05:45.311 --> 00:05:45.745
which you know

00:05:45.745 --> 00:05:47.814
a little bit about the FDIC,

00:05:47.980 --> 00:05:49.515
Treasury, in short,

00:05:49.515 --> 00:05:50.917
the Biden administration.

00:05:50.917 --> 00:05:51.384
Aren't you

00:05:51.384 --> 00:05:52.251
are you pointing the finger

00:05:52.251 --> 00:05:53.186
too much at Powell

00:05:53.186 --> 00:05:55.154
and not enough at President Biden

00:05:55.154 --> 00:05:56.823
in all the agencies and departments

00:05:56.823 --> 00:05:57.557
that he's in charge?

00:05:57.557 --> 00:05:58.891
The one who is responsible

00:05:58.891 --> 00:06:00.560
on safety and soundness.

00:06:00.560 --> 00:06:02.228
That's the part we want to go here.

00:06:02.228 --> 00:06:04.630
Is this financially solvent

00:06:04.630 --> 00:06:06.165
and stable bank?

00:06:06.165 --> 00:06:07.600
That's what the Fed

00:06:07.600 --> 00:06:08.434
for all of these

00:06:08.434 --> 00:06:11.037
$50 billion and above banks.

00:06:11.371 --> 00:06:13.439
And that's where it is that Jerome

00:06:13.439 --> 00:06:15.675
Powell has spent years now

00:06:15.675 --> 00:06:17.110
weakening the regulations.

00:06:17.110 --> 00:06:17.910
In fact,

00:06:17.910 --> 00:06:20.046
I had him at a hearing not long ago

00:06:20.380 --> 00:06:21.848
in which I talked about the fact

00:06:21.848 --> 00:06:23.282
that he has weakened

00:06:23.282 --> 00:06:25.118
the regulations over these banks

00:06:25.118 --> 00:06:26.386
not once, not twice,

00:06:26.386 --> 00:06:28.788
but literally dozens of times.

00:06:28.788 --> 00:06:31.491
And so I said to him, of all the things

00:06:31.491 --> 00:06:32.759
you've done for these banks

00:06:32.759 --> 00:06:35.161
and a lot of it's way down in the weeds,

00:06:35.161 --> 00:06:36.763
can you name just one

00:06:36.763 --> 00:06:38.264
where you kind of tightened

00:06:38.264 --> 00:06:39.565
the regulations a little bit,

00:06:39.565 --> 00:06:41.167
where you increased oversight

00:06:41.167 --> 00:06:41.601
a little bit?

00:06:41.601 --> 00:06:44.070
His answer was no, no.

00:06:44.704 --> 00:06:46.773
After the Silicon Valley bank failure,

00:06:46.773 --> 00:06:47.573
you sent a

00:06:47.573 --> 00:06:49.075
letter to the former CEO

00:06:49.075 --> 00:06:49.742
of that bank

00:06:49.742 --> 00:06:51.878
arguing that his lobbying

00:06:52.211 --> 00:06:53.746
to weaken the rules.

00:06:53.746 --> 00:06:54.881
I don't know if you mean

00:06:54.881 --> 00:06:56.549
with Congress, which actually

00:06:57.483 --> 00:06:58.317
acquiesced.

00:06:58.317 --> 00:06:58.651
Yes.

00:06:58.651 --> 00:06:59.252
In 2018,

00:06:59.252 --> 00:07:00.887
but also or also with with him

00:07:00.887 --> 00:07:03.022
with Fed Chair Powell.

00:07:03.022 --> 00:07:04.590
But but you said his lobbying

00:07:04.590 --> 00:07:06.125
is what enabled the collapse,

00:07:06.125 --> 00:07:07.427
and you asked him to submit answers

00:07:07.427 --> 00:07:09.762
to your questions by March 28th.

00:07:09.762 --> 00:07:11.731
It is not yet March 28th, I should note.

00:07:11.731 --> 00:07:12.665
Have you heard back?

00:07:12.665 --> 00:07:14.634
And what are you hoping? No, we have not.

00:07:14.634 --> 00:07:16.702
But this really is the reminder.

00:07:16.702 --> 00:07:17.837
This is not a story

00:07:17.837 --> 00:07:20.072
that just one day fell out of the sky.

00:07:20.072 --> 00:07:21.707
This is a story that starts

00:07:21.707 --> 00:07:23.142
back with you remembers

00:07:23.142 --> 00:07:25.378
the last crash put Dodd-Frank in place,

00:07:25.912 --> 00:07:27.280
promised the American people,

00:07:27.280 --> 00:07:28.748
we're going to have tough regulations

00:07:28.748 --> 00:07:30.082
and that means we're not going to have

00:07:30.082 --> 00:07:31.651
any more bank failures

00:07:31.651 --> 00:07:33.820
then these multibillion dollar banks,

00:07:33.820 --> 00:07:36.989
including the CEO of the Silicon

00:07:36.989 --> 00:07:39.625
Valley Bank, come in and say, no, no, no.

00:07:39.992 --> 00:07:41.394
They want to be treated

00:07:41.394 --> 00:07:43.830
not like the multibillion dollar banks

00:07:43.830 --> 00:07:44.630
they are.

00:07:44.630 --> 00:07:44.997
They said

00:07:44.997 --> 00:07:46.766
we're just like those little tiny

00:07:46.766 --> 00:07:48.134
local community banks

00:07:48.134 --> 00:07:49.936
that do such a great job

00:07:49.936 --> 00:07:52.205
of providing local loans and so on.

00:07:52.605 --> 00:07:55.308
So regulate us very lightly, they said,

00:07:55.541 --> 00:07:57.543
because they claimed they posed

00:07:57.543 --> 00:07:59.645
no risk to the economy.

00:08:00.112 --> 00:08:01.380
Now, Donald Trump

00:08:01.380 --> 00:08:03.549
then ran for president, saying

00:08:03.583 --> 00:08:05.117
to those banks, right,

00:08:05.117 --> 00:08:06.686
multibillion dollar banks,

00:08:06.686 --> 00:08:08.788
I will tighten regulations on you.

00:08:08.788 --> 00:08:10.323
Once he was elected,

00:08:10.323 --> 00:08:12.425
he put in regulators

00:08:12.825 --> 00:08:15.027
who believed in deregulation.

00:08:15.027 --> 00:08:16.295
Then he went to Congress

00:08:16.295 --> 00:08:17.897
and said to Congress,

00:08:17.897 --> 00:08:19.232
roll back

00:08:19.232 --> 00:08:22.268
the part of Dodd-Frank that requires

00:08:22.268 --> 00:08:25.505
more supervision over these $50 billion.

00:08:25.571 --> 00:08:27.206
And most Republicans went along with it.

00:08:27.206 --> 00:08:29.809
But also a bunch of Democrats, too. Yup.

00:08:29.809 --> 00:08:31.844
No. He got help from both parties.

00:08:32.111 --> 00:08:35.014
And then what happened is that Jerome

00:08:35.014 --> 00:08:38.017
Powell said you've opened the door

00:08:38.551 --> 00:08:41.153
for much more deregulation.

00:08:41.153 --> 00:08:43.189
Massive deregulation.

00:08:43.189 --> 00:08:44.924
And he said he's actually on the record

00:08:44.924 --> 00:08:47.593
saying this because you opened the door.

00:08:47.627 --> 00:08:50.463
I am now going to go full steam ahead

00:08:50.930 --> 00:08:52.899
and lighten the regulations.

00:08:52.899 --> 00:08:54.166
And then his

00:08:54.166 --> 00:08:56.335
then vice chair, who was Randy

00:08:56.335 --> 00:08:59.438
Quarrels, said that his job was to

00:08:59.438 --> 00:09:02.308
change the culture at the Fed

00:09:02.942 --> 00:09:04.644
in order to let these banks

00:09:04.644 --> 00:09:05.545
do what they wanted

00:09:05.545 --> 00:09:06.312
to do

00:09:06.312 --> 00:09:07.547
to be able to take on

00:09:07.547 --> 00:09:09.615
risk, run up profits.

00:09:09.615 --> 00:09:10.516
And I'm going to say

00:09:10.516 --> 00:09:11.951
he didn't add this part

00:09:11.951 --> 00:09:13.586
and run the risk of exploding.

00:09:13.586 --> 00:09:16.689
Do you want other parts of the Biden

00:09:16.689 --> 00:09:18.891
administration to be more aggressive

00:09:18.891 --> 00:09:20.293
on these issues?

00:09:20.293 --> 00:09:21.727
All of the Treasury Department

00:09:21.727 --> 00:09:23.529
and all of the other agencies and

00:09:23.529 --> 00:09:25.164
and regulatory departments

00:09:25.164 --> 00:09:25.898
that I mentioned.

00:09:25.898 --> 00:09:26.999
What do they need to be more

00:09:26.999 --> 00:09:28.367
aggressive as well?

00:09:28.367 --> 00:09:29.869
I think right now

00:09:29.869 --> 00:09:32.471
this really is at the Fed.

00:09:32.805 --> 00:09:34.574
And then I want to say the regional Fed.

00:09:34.574 --> 00:09:38.244
So the whole Fed structure, the CFP,

00:09:38.444 --> 00:09:39.679
for example,

00:09:39.679 --> 00:09:41.547
they're dealing with consumer contracts.

00:09:41.547 --> 00:09:43.583
And that's not the heart of what's gone

00:09:43.583 --> 00:09:44.817
wrong here.

00:09:44.817 --> 00:09:46.652
FDIC is trying to figure out

00:09:46.652 --> 00:09:49.188
how to manage the insurance

00:09:49.922 --> 00:09:51.157
for deposit rates.

00:09:51.157 --> 00:09:53.326
And actually, I think this is a place,

00:09:53.326 --> 00:09:55.027
thanks to the intervention,

00:09:55.027 --> 00:09:56.462
that the Treasury was forced

00:09:56.462 --> 00:09:58.531
to take weakened before last.

00:09:58.531 --> 00:09:59.765
I think this is a place now

00:09:59.765 --> 00:10:00.466
we're going to have to have

00:10:00.466 --> 00:10:02.134
statutory change

00:10:02.134 --> 00:10:04.303
because in effect, the Treasury

00:10:04.437 --> 00:10:06.238
combined with the Fed,

00:10:06.238 --> 00:10:07.673
has said we're going to come in

00:10:07.673 --> 00:10:08.174
and start

00:10:08.174 --> 00:10:11.344
backstopping all deposits, backstop

00:10:11.344 --> 00:10:12.645
ing the banks,

00:10:12.645 --> 00:10:14.013
and that means they're providing,

00:10:14.013 --> 00:10:16.082
in effect, a form of insurance

00:10:16.082 --> 00:10:18.351
and not charging for it. Hmm.

00:10:18.351 --> 00:10:22.121
Is there a way we saw some elements

00:10:22.121 --> 00:10:23.122
after the East

00:10:23.122 --> 00:10:26.359
Palestine, Ohio train derailment travesty

00:10:26.959 --> 00:10:27.526
where we saw

00:10:27.526 --> 00:10:29.929
some elements of the populist right,

00:10:30.496 --> 00:10:32.298
the JD Vance's of the world

00:10:32.298 --> 00:10:33.566
joining with some elements

00:10:33.566 --> 00:10:34.800
of the populist left,

00:10:34.800 --> 00:10:36.602
the Sherrod Browns of the world.

00:10:36.602 --> 00:10:38.604
Is there an area here

00:10:38.604 --> 00:10:40.039
for the kind of actions

00:10:40.039 --> 00:10:41.173
you're talking about

00:10:41.173 --> 00:10:43.175
that conservatives could join with you?

00:10:43.209 --> 00:10:44.744
I think there is

00:10:44.744 --> 00:10:46.612
and it's the reminder

00:10:46.612 --> 00:10:48.214
that there are regulations

00:10:48.214 --> 00:10:50.116
that are helpful to all of us

00:10:50.116 --> 00:10:52.451
and the regulations are about safety.

00:10:52.485 --> 00:10:53.152
That's what

00:10:53.152 --> 00:10:55.254
obviously the train derailment was about.

00:10:55.488 --> 00:10:57.790
It's also about economic safety.

00:10:57.790 --> 00:10:59.925
We need a Federal Reserve

00:10:59.992 --> 00:11:02.194
that is doing its job

00:11:02.194 --> 00:11:04.263
and that is to keep these banks safe.

00:11:04.263 --> 00:11:04.830
Look,

00:11:04.830 --> 00:11:06.032
no depositor, no

00:11:06.032 --> 00:11:09.001
small business, no family, individual

00:11:09.368 --> 00:11:10.336
should have to say,

00:11:10.336 --> 00:11:11.337
I need to see the bank's

00:11:11.337 --> 00:11:13.039
balance sheet before

00:11:13.039 --> 00:11:14.306
I know that it's safe

00:11:14.306 --> 00:11:15.841
to put money in the bank.

00:11:15.841 --> 00:11:17.610
The whole idea is

00:11:17.610 --> 00:11:18.811
the regulators

00:11:18.811 --> 00:11:21.480
are supposed to keep those banks safe.

00:11:21.781 --> 00:11:22.214
You know,

00:11:22.214 --> 00:11:24.650
I used to talk about exploding toasters

00:11:25.051 --> 00:11:25.851
that you shouldn't

00:11:25.851 --> 00:11:27.820
have to be an expert on toasters

00:11:27.820 --> 00:11:28.888
to buy a toaster.

00:11:28.888 --> 00:11:30.756
Yeah, we ought to know that they're safe.

00:11:30.756 --> 00:11:32.792
That's what regulations are about.

00:11:32.792 --> 00:11:34.193
Same thing ought to be true

00:11:34.193 --> 00:11:35.895
about putting money in banks.

00:11:35.895 --> 00:11:37.263
It should be safe.

00:11:37.263 --> 00:11:38.097
Banking

00:11:38.097 --> 00:11:40.966
should not be a place for risk takers

00:11:41.400 --> 00:11:42.301
who want to.

00:11:42.301 --> 00:11:43.669
Who want to build up,

00:11:43.669 --> 00:11:45.171
you know, fast profits.

00:11:45.171 --> 00:11:46.605
Silicon Valley Bank.

00:11:46.605 --> 00:11:49.275
Increase their profitability by 40%

00:11:49.275 --> 00:11:51.077
the last three years.

00:11:51.077 --> 00:11:52.878
That's not what we want from banks.

00:11:52.878 --> 00:11:54.947
We want banks that are boring

00:11:54.947 --> 00:11:55.848
and that are safe.

